Felicity Huffman spotted for the first  time since serving her federal prison  sentence after turning herself in  Tuesday morning the actress's photo was  snapped during a visit with husband  William H Macy and her daughter on  Saturday  Huffman can be seen in her dark green  prison uniform and a white ball cap the  56 year old started her prison sentence  earlier this week for her role in the  College Admission scandal EG learned on  Wednesday that Huffman received credit  for one day of her 14-day prison  sentence that accounted for the time she  spent in custody after her arrest in  March in addition to her prison time  Huffman was also sentenced to one year  of supervised release a 30 thousand  dollar fine in 250 hours of community  service at the time of her sentencing  Huffman released a statement that read  in part quote I'm in full acceptance of  my guilt then with deep regret and shame  over what I've done the mother of two  will remain behind bars for the duration  of her sentence at the Federal  Correctional Institute in Dublin  California  [Music]  [Applause]
 

